id: design.durable-timeout
kind: design
title: durable timeouts (outliving the process)
aliases: durable timeout, durable timer, durable deadline, externalized timeout
tags: design, timeouts, async, durability
questions:
  - how do you time something out if the process may die?
  - when is a timeout not in memory?
invariant: A timeout that must outlive a process or a host failure is externalized — stored in a queue, a lease, or a database — not held in RAM.
answer_30s: Externalize the deadline (a message with a delivery time, a row with an expires_at, a lease with a TTL); workers poll for work and the system decides staleness from the durable clock, not from an in-process timer.
when_to_use:
  - background jobs, queues, and scheduled work
  - any timeout that gates customer-visible work across a deploy
avoid_when:
  - the work is single-host, in-process, and short-lived
related:
  - design.graceful-shutdown
  - recipe.async-job-processing
  - design.timeouts
sources:
  - https://sre.google/sre-book/
